 <h2 id="dub-long">Dub Long Video</h2>
+<div class="card"><h3>Also analyse the picture</h3><p>New video projects can use the picture as another check of who speaks. You can switch this off before accepting the estimate. Its credit cost is listed separately; failed portions are refunded. Audio-only files do not use it. Shot-cut detection is free. Unclear pictures give no speaker answer. When the picture shows clearly, in several lines and every time the same, that a speaker is male or female, that gender is set before the translation; when it is less clear, you are only told to check. Your own choice of voice or gender is never changed.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><h3>What is Dub Long Video?</h3><p>A separate page (🎞️ Dub Long Video in the app, or /dub-long) for videos of several minutes — much longer than the <span data-limit="short_max_sec">30</span>-second limit of the normal dub (<span data-limit="short_lipsync_max_sec">15</span> seconds with lip-sync). It is available to every user (you pay for each job with your credits). A long dub takes a video of <span data-limit="long_min_sec">20</span> seconds up to <span data-limit="long_max_min">60</span> minutes, in a file of up to <span data-limit="long_max_upload_mb">2048</span> MB. That is the size of one upload; the storage space of your plan is a separate limit and only decides how long finished files stay. It works in the background: you can close the page, and we email you when your dubbed file is ready.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><h3>Fix wrong words with a subtitle file</h3><p>When you start a project (or later, on the estimate page before you accept it) you can add a subtitle in the video's original language file of the video (SRT, VTT, SBV or ASS). After the speech is transcribed, and before the translation, Lisan AI finds your video's speech inside the subtitle - it can be the subtitle of a whole film, with different times - and puts the subtitle's wording into your lines, so names and wrong words are fixed and the Arabic is made from the corrected original text. Everything in the subtitle outside your video is ignored. You choose how lines are written: Smart (a new line where the subtitle shows another speaker), Together, or Separate (one line per subtitle line). If the subtitle cannot be matched, the transcript stays as the AI heard it and you are told. It costs nothing.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><h3>Glossary: keep names and terms the same</h3><p>In Dub Long Video you can add a glossary: names, places, brands or technical words that must always be written the same way in Arabic. Open "Glossary (optional)" on the estimate page (before you accept, so the first translation already follows it) or in the review step, and write one term per line as <strong>Original = Arabic</strong>, for example <em>Neo = نيو</em>. In the review step the button "Apply to the lines" translates again only the lines that contain one of your terms but don't use it. Lines you typed yourself are never changed. The glossary is free and it is kept when you redo a project.</p></div>
